meta {
  name: 06 Simulate provider webhook
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/payments
  body: text
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  x-fake-signature: bc0d49a8b9dc2670c729c0da2c6fc27a07b30d14b78666d4cef138277cd35ae8
}

body:text {
  {"reference":"fake_2e67550a-b132-4f4a-88fd-1260c67b1c0b","outcome":"SUCCEEDED"}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.received: eq true
}

docs {
  Bruno Desktop often cannot `require('crypto')`. Set body + `x-fake-signature`
  by hand.
  
  For payment d9b8df1e-7790-4257-8b84-f2c2df3614e4 with secret
  `local-fake-webhook-secret-at-least-32-chars`:
  
  Body (exact):
  {"reference":"fake_d9b8df1e-7790-4257-8b84-f2c2df3614e4","outcome":"SUCCEEDED"}
  
  Header x-fake-signature:
  bea8220696fc8bd4765130b4c026c0ef1da755ed135e8415fd0d7c771859bde6
  
  Prerequisites:
  1. Server: PAYMENT_PROVIDER=fake + FAKE_PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET matching
     Bruno fakeWebhookSecret (≥32 chars).
  2. DB: provider_reference = fake_<paymentId> on that payment row.
  
  Expected: { "received": true, "outcome": "ACTIVATED" }
  
  Regenerate for another paymentId:
  node -e "const c=require('crypto');const id='PAYMENT_ID';const secret='local-fake-webhook-secret-at-least-32-chars';const raw=JSON.stringify({reference:'fake_'+id,outcome:'SUCCEEDED'});console.log(raw);console.log(c.createHmac('sha256',secret).update(raw).digest('hex'));"
}
